Assumed, not sourced: the `git diff <orig> HEAD` check assumes every
group gets committed. When part of the change is meant to be dropped
(git-rebase-i's removal case), the diff shows exactly that part, which
is still a useful check but not an empty one.

The reason for -N is the appendix's, reworded from "instead of
dropping them to untracked" to "all the way to untracked" to match
the message of the commit that added it.
